			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὐπρεπὲς ἄσπονδον προβέβληνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. σκῆψιν, πρόφασιν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.56.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.20.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in 
				Att.
			 law, <i>accuse</i> a person by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προβολή</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προβολή</span>
			v), <i>present him as guilty</i> of the offence, 
